<title>VENEZUELA: SOCCER-BORRERO NAMES VENEZUELA COACH.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-BORRERO NAMES VENEZUELA COACH.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eduardo Borrero was named Venezuela national team coach on Monday.</p>
<p>Borrero, in charge of  first division Mineros de Guayana, replaced Rafael Santana, who was sacked last week following Venezuela's poor World Cup results.</p>
<p>Venezuela have lost all hope of reaching the finals, languishing ninth and last in the South American qualifying group with five defeats and one draw.</p>
<p>Borrero's first game will be a friendly against Costa Rica on November 27.</p>
</text>
